    'Repeat this process for any properties that you think are potential gadgets.' => 'Ulangi untuk setiap properti kandidat lainnya.',
    'Finding client-side prototype pollution gadgets using DOM Invader' => 'Menemukan gadget sisi klien memakai DOM Invader',
    'As you can see from the previous steps, manually identifying prototype pollution gadgets in the wild can be a laborious task. Given that websites often rely on a number of third-party libraries, this may involve reading through thousands of lines of minified or obfuscated code, which makes things even trickier. DOM Invader can automatically scan for gadgets on your behalf and can even generate a DOM XSS proof-of-concept in some cases. This means you can find exploits on real-world sites in a matter of seconds rather than hours.' => 'Menelaah kode ter-minify secara manual sangat menyita waktu; DOM Invader mengotomatiskan pencarian gadget sekaligus menghasilkan PoC DOM XSS dalam hitungan detik.',
    'For more information, check out [[A0]]Scanning for prototype pollution gadgets with DOM Invader[[/A0]].' => 'Pelajari caranya pada [[A0]]Memindai gadget prototype pollution dengan DOM Invader[[/A0]].',
    'Prototype pollution via the constructor' => 'Prototype pollution melalui constructor',
    "So far, we've looked exclusively at how you can get a reference to prototype objects via the special [[C0]] accessor property. As this is the classic technique for prototype pollution, a common defense is to strip any properties with the key [[C1]] from user-controlled objects before merging them. This approach is flawed as there are alternative ways to reference [[C2]] without relying on the [[C3]] string at all." => 'Filter yang sekadar menghapus kunci [[C0]] dan [[C1]] tidaklah cukup karena referensi ke [[C2]] masih dapat dicapai tanpa kata kunci [[C3]].',
    "Unless its [[A0]]prototype is set to [[C0]][[/A0]], every JavaScript object has a [[C1]] property, which contains a reference to the constructor function that was used to create it. For example, you can create a new object either using literal syntax or by explicitly invoking the [[C2]] constructor as follows:" => 'Selama [[A0]]prototipenya tidak diatur ke [[C0]][[/A0]], setiap objek memiliki properti [[C1]] yang menunjuk ke fungsi pembangunnya seperti [[C2]]:',
    'You can then reference the [[C0]] constructor via the built-in [[C1]] property:' => 'Fungsi pembangun [[C0]] diakses melalui properti [[C1]] seperti ini:',
    "Remember that functions are also just objects under the hood. Each constructor function has a [[C0]] property, which points to the prototype that will be assigned to any objects that are created by this constructor. As a result, you can also access any object's prototype as follows:" => 'Setiap fungsi konstruktor memiliki properti [[C0]] yang menunjuk langsung ke prototipe objek buatannya:',
    'As [[C0]] is equivalent to [[C1]], this provides an alternative vector for prototype pollution.' => 'Karena [[C0]] setara dengan [[C1]], jalur ini menjadi vektor bypass yang efektif.',
    'Bypassing flawed key sanitization' => 'Melewati sanitasi kunci yang cacat',
    'An obvious way in which websites attempt to prevent prototype pollution is by sanitizing property keys before merging them into an existing object. However, a common mistake is failing to recursively sanitize the input string. For example, consider the following URL:' => 'Jika filter hanya menghapus kata kunci satu kali tanpa rekursi, payload bersarang seperti berikut dapat lolos:',
    'If the sanitization process just strips the string [[C0]] without repeating this process more than once, this would result in the following URL, which is a potentially valid prototype pollution source:' => 'Begitu substring [[C0]] di tengah dihapus sekali, potongan di kanan dan kiri bergabung membentuk kunci valid:',
    'Prototype pollution in external libraries' => 'Prototype pollution di pustaka eksternal',
    "As we've touched on already, prototype pollution gadgets may occur in third-party libraries that are imported by the application. In this case, we strongly recommend using DOM Invader's prototype pollution features to identify sources and gadgets. Not only is this much quicker, it also ensures you won't miss vulnerabilities that would otherwise be extremely tricky to notice." => 'Gadget sering bersembunyi di dalam pustaka pihak ketiga yang diimpor situs; pemindaian otomatis memudahkan pendeteksiannya secara menyeluruh.',
    'SecDevLab Research discovered a number of widespread prototype pollution gadgets in the JavaScript APIs commonly provided in browsers. Learn how these potentially enable you to bypass weak prototype pollution defences for DOM XSS.' => 'Pelajari gadget bawaan pada API peramban standar yang dapat menembus mitigasi parsial:',
    '[[A0]][[S0]]LABS[[/S0]] Client-side prototype pollution via browser APIs[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]][[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]] Prototype pollution sisi klien via API peramban[[/A0]]',

    // Browser APIs page
    "You may be surprised to learn that there are a number of widespread prototype pollution gadgets in the JavaScript APIs commonly provided in browsers. In this section, we'll show you how to exploit these for [[A0]]DOM XSS[[/A0]], potentially bypassing flawed prototype pollution defenses implemented by developers." => 'Sejumlah API JavaScript bawaan peramban ternyata ikut mengandung gadget prototype pollution yang dapat dieksploitasi untuk [[A0]]DOM XSS[[/A0]] sekalipun pertahanan parsial telah diterapkan.',
    'The labs in this section are based on original SecDevLab research. For a technical insight into how we were able to discover these gadgets and more using DOM Invader, check out the related blog post.' => 'Materi ini berangkat dari riset orisinal mengenai temuan gadget di API peramban standar.',
    '[[A0]]Widespread prototype pollution gadgets by Gareth Heyes[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Widespread prototype pollution gadgets oleh Gareth Heyes[[/A0]]',
    'Prototype pollution via fetch()' => 'Prototype pollution melalui fetch()',
    'The [[C0]] API provides a simple way for developers to trigger HTTP requests using JavaScript. The [[C1]] method accepts two arguments:' => 'API [[C0]] memicu permintaan HTTP lewat JavaScript dan metode [[C1]] menerima dua argumen:',
    'The URL to which you want to send the request.' => 'URL tujuan permintaan HTTP.',
    'An options object that lets you to control parts of the request, such as the method, headers, body parameters, and so on.' => 'Objek opsi untuk mengatur metode, header, badan permintaan, dan pengaturan lain.',
    'The following is an example of how you might send a [[C0]] request using [[C1]]:' => 'Contoh pengiriman permintaan [[C0]] dengan [[C1]]:',
    "As you can see, we've explicitly defined [[C0]] and [[C1]] properties, but there are a number of other possible properties that we've left undefined. In this case, if an attacker can find a suitable source, they could potentially pollute [[C2]] with their own [[C3]] property. This may then be inherited by the options object passed into [[C4]] and subsequently used to generate the request." => 'Karena [[C0]] dan [[C1]] saja yang ditentukan sementara properti seperti [[C3]] dibiarkan kosong, pencemaran [[C2]] dapat menyuntikkan header atau properti lain ke panggilan [[C4]].',
    'This can lead to a number of issues. For example, the following code is potentially vulnerable to DOM XSS via prototype pollution:' => 'Kode berikut rentan memicu DOM XSS saat properti respons berasal dari header suntikan:',
    'To exploit this, an attacker could pollute [[C0]] with a [[C1]] property containing a malicious [[C2]] header as follows:' => 'Penyerang mencemari [[C0]] lewat properti [[C1]] berisi header [[C2]] berbahaya:',
    "Let's assume that server-side, this header is used to set the value of the [[C0]] property in the returned JSON file. In the vulnerable client-side code above, this is then assigned to the [[C1]] variable, which is later passed into the [[C2]] sink, resulting in DOM XSS." => 'Jika server memantulkan [[C0]] di respons JSON, nilainya dibaca variabel [[C1]] lalu masuk ke sink [[C2]] dan memicu XSS.',
    'You can use this technique to control any undefined properties of the options object passed to [[C0]]. This may enable you to add a malicious body to the request, for example.' => 'Teknik ini berlaku bagi properti opsi [[C0]] apa pun yang tidak didefinisikan secara eksplisit, termasuk isi body permintaan.',
    'Prototype pollution via Object.defineProperty()' => 'Prototype pollution melalui Object.defineProperty()',
    'Developers with some knowledge of prototype pollution may attempt to block potential gadgets by using the [[C0]] method. This enables you to set a non-configurable, non-writable property directly on the affected object as follows:' => 'Pengembang terkadang mengunci properti objek memakai [[C0]] agar tidak mewarisi prototipe, namun tanpa menetapkan nilai awal:',
    'This may initially seem like a reasonable mitigation attempt as this prevents the vulnerable object from inheriting a malicious version of the gadget property via the prototype chain. However, this approach is inherently flawed.' => 'Sayangnya pendekatan ini memiliki celah besar apabila properti value tidak ikut diatur.',
    'Just like the [[C0]] method we looked at earlier, [[C1]] accepts an options object, known as a "descriptor". You can see this in the example above. Among other things, developers can use this descriptor object to set an initial value for the property that\'s being defined. However, if the only reason that they\'re defining this property is to protect against prototype pollution, they might not bother setting a value at all.' => 'Metode [[C1]] menerima objek descriptor yang sama seperti opsi [[C0]]. Jika pengembang lupa mendefinisikan properti value di descriptor tersebut, nilainya tetap diwarisi.',
    'In this case, an attacker may be able to bypass this defense by polluting [[C0]] with a malicious [[C1]] property. If this is inherited by the descriptor object passed to [[C2]], the attacker-controlled value may be assigned to the gadget property after all.' => 'Dengan mencemari [[C0]] memakai properti [[C1]], descriptor yang dikirim ke [[C2]] mewarisi nilai penyerang tersebut.',
    "JavaScript is now commonly used to build back-end functionality. Naturally, this means that prototype pollution can also occur in server-side contexts. In the next section, you'll learn how to safely detect and exploit these vulnerabilities in applications running on Node.js." => 'JavaScript kini luas dipakai di sisi server (Node.js). Bagian selanjutnya mengulas teknik deteksi aman serta eksploitasi prototype pollution sisi server.',
    '[[A0]][[S0]]LABS[[/S0]] Server-side prototype pollution[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]][[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]] Prototype pollution sisi server[[/A0]]',

    // Server-side page
    "JavaScript was originally a client-side language designed to run in browsers. However, due to the emergence of server-side runtimes, such as the hugely popular Node.js, JavaScript is now widely used to build servers, APIs, and other back-end applications. Logically, this means that it's also possible for prototype pollution vulnerabilities to arise in server-side contexts." => 'Dengan populernya runtime seperti Node.js, JavaScript dipakai membangun API dan layanan backend sehingga kerentanan prototype pollution juga hadir di sisi server.',
    'Although the fundamental concepts remain largely the same, the process of identifying server-side prototype pollution vulnerabilities, and developing them into working exploits, presents some additional challenges.' => 'Meski prinsip dasarnya sama, pengujian serta eksploitasi di sisi server memiliki tantangan teknis tersendiri.',
    "In this section, you'll learn a number of techniques for black-box detection of server-side prototype pollution. We'll cover how to do this efficiently and non-destructively, then use interactive, deliberately vulnerable labs to demonstrate how you can leverage prototype pollution for remote code execution." => 'Anda akan mempelajari metode deteksi blackbox secara non-destruktif tanpa melumpuhkan server serta jalur eskalasi ke RCE di Node.js.',
    'Some of the materials and labs in this section are based on original SecDevLab research. For more technical details and an insight into how we were able to develop these techniques, check out the accompanying whitepaper by Gareth Heyes:' => 'Materi berikut merujuk riset teknis terkait pendeteksian prototype pollution sisi server tanpa DoS:',
    '[[A0]]Server-side prototype pollution: Black-box detection without the DoS[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Server-side prototype pollution: Black-box detection without the DoS[[/A0]]',
    'Why is server-side prototype pollution more difficult to detect?' => 'Mengapa prototype pollution sisi server lebih sulit dideteksi?',
    'For a number of reasons, server-side prototype pollution is generally more difficult to detect than its client-side variant:' => 'Terdapat empat hambatan utama saat menguji target sisi server secara blackbox:',
    '<strong>No source code access</strong> - Unlike with client-side vulnerabilities, you typically won\'t have access to the vulnerable JavaScript. This means there\'s no easy way to get an overview of which sinks are present or spot potential gadget properties.' => '<strong>Tanpa akses kode sumber</strong> - Anda tidak dapat langsung melihat kode JavaScript backend untuk mencari gadget maupun sink.',
    "<strong>Lack of developer tools</strong> - As the JavaScript is running on a remote system, you don't have the ability to inspect objects at runtime like you would when using your browser's DevTools to inspect the DOM. This means it can be hard to tell when you've successfully polluted the prototype unless you've caused a noticeable change in the website's behavior. This limitation obviously doesn't apply to white-box testing." => '<strong>Tidak ada konsol runtime</strong> - Penguji tidak bisa memeriksa isi memori objek saat runtime layaknya di DevTools peramban.',
    "<strong>The DoS problem</strong> - Successfully polluting objects in a server-side environment using real properties often breaks application functionality or brings down the server completely. As it's easy to inadvertently cause a denial-of-service (DoS), testing in production can be dangerous. Even if you do identify a vulnerability, developing this into an exploit is also tricky when you've essentially broken the site in the process." => '<strong>Risiko DoS tinggi</strong> - Mencemari properti penting secara sembarangan dapat langsung menjatuhkan proses server.',
    "<strong>Pollution persistence</strong> - When testing in a browser, you can reverse all of your changes and get a clean environment again by simply refreshing the page. Once you pollute a server-side prototype, this change persists for the entire lifetime of the Node process and you don't have any way of resetting it." => '<strong>Sifat persisten selama proses hidup</strong> - Sekali prototipe Node.js tercemar, perubahannya bertahan hingga layanan direstart, tidak hilang dengan muat ulang halaman.',
    "In the following sections, we'll cover a number of non-destructive techniques that enable you to safely test for server-side prototype pollution despite these limitations." => 'Oleh sebab itu, gunakan teknik deteksi aman berikut.',
    'Detecting server-side prototype pollution via polluted property reflection' => 'Mendeteksi melalui pantulan properti tercemar',
    "An easy trap for developers to fall into is forgetting or overlooking the fact that a JavaScript [[C0]] loop iterates over all of an object's enumerable properties, including ones that it has inherited via the prototype chain." => 'Perulangan JavaScript [[C0]] menelusuri seluruh properti enumerable pada objek termasuk properti warisan dari prototipe.',
    "This doesn't include built-in properties set by JavaScript's native constructors as these are non-enumerable by default." => 'Properti bawaan konstruktor native bersifat non-enumerable, sedangkan properti yang kita suntikkan ke Object.prototype bersifat enumerable.',
    'You can test this out for yourself as follows:' => 'Contoh perilaku iterasi tersebut terlihat di bawah ini:',
    'This also applies to arrays, where a [[C0]] loop first iterates over each index, which is essentially just a numeric property key under the hood, before moving on to any inherited properties as well.' => 'Hal yang sama berlaku untuk array saat diiterasi dengan [[C0]]:',
    'In either case, if the application later includes the returned properties in a response, this can provide a simple way to probe for server-side prototype pollution.' => 'Jika server menyalin atau mengembalikan properti hasil iterasi itu ke respons JSON, pencemaran langsung tampak.',
    "[[C0]] or [[C1]] requests that submit JSON data to an application or API are prime candidates for this kind of behavior as it's common for servers to respond with a JSON representation of the new or updated object. In this case, you could attempt to pollute the global [[C2]] with an arbitrary property as follows:" => 'Endpoint [[C0]] atau [[C1]] yang membalas objek JSON hasil pembaruan adalah target ideal untuk menguji pencemaran [[C2]]:',
    'If the website is vulnerable, your injected property would then appear in the updated object in the response:' => 'Jika rentan, properti suntikan muncul di respons JSON pembaruan profil:',
    'In rare cases, the website may even use these properties to dynamically generate HTML, resulting in the injected property being rendered in your browser.' => 'Terkadang properti tercemar tersebut ikut dirender ke dalam halaman HTML.',
    'Once you identify that server-side prototype pollution is possible, you can then look for potential gadgets to use for an exploit. Any features that involve updating user data are worth investigating as these often involve merging the incoming data into an existing object that represents the user within the application. If you can add arbitrary properties to your own user, this can potentially lead to a number of vulnerabilities, including privilege escalation.' => 'Fitur pembaruan profil akun sering menggabungkan JSON ke objek pengguna sehingga berpotensi menaikkan hak akses bila properti seperti peran atau status admin tercemar.',
    'Detecting server-side prototype pollution without polluted property reflection' => 'Mendeteksi tanpa pantulan properti tercemar',
    "Most of the time, even when you successfully pollute a server-side prototype object, you won't see the affected property reflected in a response. Given that you can't just inspect the object in a console either, this presents a challenge when trying to tell whether your injection worked." => 'Sering kali properti uji tidak dipantulkan di respons JSON sehingga diperlukan pengamatan perubahan perilaku server.',
    "One approach is to try injecting properties that match potential configuration options for the server. You can then compare the server's behavior before and after the injection to see whether this configuration change appears to have taken effect. If so, this is a strong indication that you've successfully found a server-side prototype pollution vulnerability." => 'Caranya adalah menyuntikkan opsi konfigurasi aman lalu membandingkan respons sebelum dan sesudah pencemaran.',
    "In this section, we'll look at the following techniques:" => 'Tiga teknik deteksi non-destruktif yang dibahas:',
    '[[A0]]Status code override[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Penimpaan kode status HTTP[[/A0]]',
    '[[A0]]JSON spaces override[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Penimpaan spasi indentasi JSON[[/A0]]',
    '[[A0]]Charset override[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Penimpaan charset permintaan[[/A0]]',
    'All of these injections are non-destructive, but still produce a consistent and distinctive change in server behavior when successful. You can use any of the techniques covered in this section to solve the [[A0]]accompanying lab[[/A0]].' => 'Ketiganya aman tanpa merusak layanan dan dapat dipakai untuk menyelesaikan [[A0]]lab terkait[[/A0]].',
    "This is just a small selection of potential techniques to give you an idea of what's possible. For more technical details and an insight into how SecDevLab Research was able to develop these techniques, check out the accompanying whitepaper [[A0]]Server-side prototype pollution: Black-box detection without the DoS by Gareth Heyes[[/A0]]." => 'Untuk detail riset lebih lengkap, baca makalah [[A0]]Server-side prototype pollution: Black-box detection without the DoS oleh Gareth Heyes[[/A0]].',
    'Status code override' => 'Penimpaan kode status HTTP',
    'Server-side JavaScript frameworks like Express allow developers to set custom HTTP response statuses. In the case of errors, a JavaScript server may issue a generic HTTP response, but include an error object in JSON format in the body. This is one way of providing additional details about why an error occurred, which may not be obvious from the default HTTP status.' => 'Framework Node.js seperti Express sering membalas error JSON lewat modul pembantu status HTTP.',
    "Although it's somewhat misleading, it's even fairly common to receive a [[C0]] response, only for the response body to contain an error object with a different status." => 'Terkadang respons memakai status [[C0]] sementara isi JSON mencantumkan kode error sebenarnya:',
    "Node's [[C0]] module contains the following function for generating this kind of error response:" => 'Modul [[C0]] membaca properti status dari objek error seperti terlihat di bawah ini:',
    "The first highlighted line attempts to assign the [[C0]] variable by reading the [[C1]] or [[C2]] property from the object passed into the function. If the website's developers haven't explicitly set a [[C3]] property for the error, you can potentially use this to probe for prototype pollution as follows:" => 'Jika properti [[C3]] (atau [[C1]]/[[C2]]) tidak ditetapkan eksplisit pada error, [[C0]] akan diwarisi lewat prototipe:',
    'Find a way to trigger an error response and take note of the default status code.' => 'Picu respons error (misalnya JSON invalid) dan catat kode status bawaannya.',
    'Try polluting the prototype with your own [[C0]] property. Be sure to use an obscure status code that is unlikely to be issued for any other reason.' => 'Cemari prototipe memakai properti [[C0]] dengan kode unik.',
    "Trigger the error response again and check whether you've successfully overridden the status code." => 'Picu error yang sama kembali dan amati apakah kode status HTTP berubah.',
    "You must choose a status code in the [[C0]]-[[C1]] range. Otherwise, Node defaults to a [[C2]] status regardless, as you can see from the second highlighted line, so you won't know whether you've polluted the prototype or not." => 'Pilih kode dalam rentang [[C0]] sampai [[C1]] agar Node tidak menimpanya menjadi [[C2]].',
    'JSON spaces override' => 'Penimpaan spasi indentasi JSON',
    "The Express framework provides a [[C0]] option, which enables you to configure the number of spaces used to indent any JSON data in the response. In many cases, developers leave this property undefined as they're happy with the default value, making it susceptible to pollution via the prototype chain." => 'Express memiliki opsi [[C0]] untuk mengatur jumlah spasi indentasi output JSON yang kerap dibiarkan undefined.',
    "If you've got access to any kind of JSON response, you can try polluting the prototype with your own [[C0]] property, then reissue the relevant request to see if the indentation in the JSON increases accordingly. You can perform the same steps to remove the indentation in order to confirm the vulnerability." => 'Mencemari [[C0]] lalu memanggil endpoint JSON akan mengubah indentasi respons; mengembalikannya ke nilai awal juga langsung membuktikan kendali kita.',
    "This is an especially useful technique because it doesn't rely on a specific property being reflected. It's also extremely safe as you're effectively able to turn the pollution on and off simply by resetting the property to the same value as the default." => 'Teknik ini sangat aman karena perubahannya mudah diaktifkan maupun dinormalkan kembali.',
    "Although the prototype pollution has been fixed in Express 4.17.4, websites that haven't upgraded may still be vulnerable." => 'Walau sudah ditambal sejak Express 4.17.4, versi lebih lama tetap terpengaruh.',
    "When attempting this technique in Burp, remember to switch to the message editor's <strong>Raw</strong> tab. Otherwise, you won't be able to see the indentation change as the default prettified view normalizes this." => 'Gunakan tab tampilan <strong>Raw</strong> di editor respons karena tab Pretty otomatis memformat ulang spasi JSON.',
    'Charset override' => 'Penimpaan charset permintaan',
    'Express servers often implement so-called "middleware" modules that enable preprocessing of requests before they\'re passed to the appropriate handler function. For example, the [[C0]] module is commonly used to parse the body of incoming requests in order to generate a [[C1]] object. This contains another gadget that you can use to probe for server-side prototype pollution.' => 'Middleware seperti [[C0]] mem-parsing badan permintaan ke [[C1]] dan membaca konfigurasi charset secara rentan:',
    'Notice that the following code passes an options object into the [[C0]] function, which is used to read in the request body for parsing. One of these options, [[C1]], determines which character encoding to use. This is either derived from the request itself via the [[C2]] function call, or it defaults to UTF-8.' => 'Fungsi [[C0]] mengambil parameter [[C1]] dari hasil [[C2]] sebelum beralih ke bawaan UTF-8:',
    "If you look closely at the [[C0]] function, it looks like the developers have anticipated that the [[C1]] header may not contain an explicit [[C2]] attribute, so they've implemented some logic that reverts to an empty string in this case. Crucially, this means it may be controllable via prototype pollution." => 'Saat header [[C1]] tidak mencantumkan [[C2]], fungsi [[C0]] bergantung pada pewarisan prototipe jika tercemar.',
    "If you can find an object whose properties are visible in a response, you can use this to probe for sources. In the following example, we'll use UTF-7 encoding and a JSON source." => 'Dengan memanfaatkan penyandian UTF-7, kita dapat menguji apakah charset berhasil ditimpa:',
    'Add an arbitrary UTF-7 encoded string to a property that\'s reflected in a response. For example, [[C0]] in UTF-7 is [[C1]].' => 'Kirimkan string bersandi UTF-7 pada properti yang dipantulkan, misalnya [[C0]] ditulis sebagai [[C1]]:',
    "Send the request. Servers won't use UTF-7 encoding by default, so this string should appear in the response in its encoded form." => 'Awalnya server tidak memakai UTF-7 sehingga respons masih memuat string tersandi mentah.',
    'Try to pollute the prototype with a [[C0]] property that explicitly specifies the UTF-7 character set:' => 'Cemari prototipe memakai properti [[C0]] yang menetapkan charset UTF-7:',
    'Repeat the first request. If you successfully polluted the prototype, the UTF-7 string should now be decoded in the response:' => 'Kirim ulang permintaan pertama; jika berhasil, string UTF-7 kini terdekode di respons:',
    "Due to a bug in Node's [[C0]] module, this works even when the request's actual [[C1]] header includes its own [[C2]] attribute. To avoid overwriting properties when a request contains duplicate headers, the [[C3]] function checks that no property already exists with the same key before transferring properties to an [[C4]] object" => 'Akibat bug pada modul [[C0]], pemeriksaan duplikat di [[C3]] untuk objek [[C4]] mengecek prototipe sehingga mengabaikan header [[C1]] dan [[C2]] asli permintaan:',
    'If it does, the header being processed is effectively dropped. Due to the way this is implemented, this check (presumably unintentionally) includes properties inherited via the prototype chain. This means that if we pollute the prototype with our own [[C0]] property, the property representing the real [[C1]] header from the request is dropped at this point, along with the intended value derived from the header.' => 'Karena properti [[C0]] sudah ada di rantai prototipe, header [[C1]] dari klien diabaikan dan digantikan oleh nilai prototipe kita.',
    'Scanning for server-side prototype pollution sources' => 'Memindai source prototype pollution sisi server',
    "Although it's useful to try manually probing for sources in order to solidify your understanding of the vulnerability, this can be repetitive and time-consuming in practice. For this reason, we've created the [[A0]]Server-Side Prototype Pollution Scanner[[/A0]] extension for Burp Suite, which enables you to automate this process. The basic workflow is as follows:" => 'Ekstensi [[A0]]Server-Side Prototype Pollution Scanner[[/A0]] mengotomatiskan teknik deteksi aman di atas melalui alur berikut:',
    'Install the <strong>Server-Side Prototype Pollution Scanner</strong> extension from the BApp Store and make sure that it is enabled. For details on how to do this, see [[A0]]Installing extensions from the BApp Store[[/A0]]' => 'Pasang ekstensi <strong>Server-Side Prototype Pollution Scanner</strong> dari BApp Store (lihat [[A0]]Memasang ekstensi[[/A0]]).',
    "Explore the target website using Burp's browser to map as much of the content as possible and accumulate traffic in the proxy history." => 'Jelajahi situs target memakai peramban untuk mengumpulkan riwayat lalu lintas API dan formulir.',
    'In Burp, go to the <strong>Proxy > HTTP history</strong> tab.' => 'Buka tab <strong>Proxy > HTTP history</strong>.',
    'Filter the list to show only in-scope items.' => 'Saring daftar agar hanya menampilkan target dalam cakupan.',
    'Select all items in the list.' => 'Pilih seluruh item yang relevan.',
    'Right-click your selection and go to <strong>Extensions > Server-Side Prototype Pollution Scanner > Server-Side Prototype Pollution</strong>, then select one of the scanning techniques from the list.' => 'Klik kanan lalu pilih menu <strong>Extensions > Server-Side Prototype Pollution Scanner > Server-Side Prototype Pollution</strong> dan pilih metode pemindaian.',
    'When prompted, modify the attack configuration if required, then click <strong>OK</strong> to launch the scan.' => 'Sesuaikan konfigurasi bila perlu lalu klik <strong>OK</strong> untuk memulai.',
    "In Burp Suite Professional, the extension reports any prototype pollution sources it finds via the <strong>Issue activity</strong> panel on the <strong>Dashboard</strong> and <strong>Target</strong> tabs. If you're using Burp Suite Community Edition, you need to go to the <strong>Extensions > Installed</strong> tab, select the extension, then monitor its <strong>Output</strong> tab for any reported issues." => 'Hasil temuan tampil pada panel <strong>Issue activity</strong> di Dashboard atau pada tab <strong>Output</strong> ekstensi.',
    "If you're unsure which scanning technique to use, you can also select <strong>Full scan</strong> to run a scan using all of the available techniques. However, this will involve sending significantly more requests." => 'Opsi <strong>Full scan</strong> menjalankan seluruh teknik deteksi sekaligus namun mengirimkan lebih banyak permintaan.',
    'Bypassing input filters for server-side prototype pollution' => 'Melewati filter masukan pada prototype pollution sisi server',
    'Websites often attempt to prevent or patch prototype pollution vulnerabilities by filtering suspicious keys like [[C0]]. This key sanitization approach is not a robust long-term solution as there are a number of ways it can potentially be bypassed. For example, an attacker can:' => 'Pemfilteran kunci seperti [[C0]] saja tidak cukup aman karena tetap bisa ditembus lewat:',
    'Obfuscate the prohibited keywords so they\'re missed during the sanitization. For more information, see [[A0]]Bypassing flawed key sanitization[[/A0]].' => 'Menyamarkan kata kunci terlarang dengan teknik penyisipan bersarang ([[A0]]Melewati sanitasi kunci yang cacat[[/A0]]).',
    'Access the prototype via the constructor property instead of [[C0]]. For more information, see [[A0]]Prototype pollution via the constructor[[/A0]]' => 'Mengakses prototipe lewat properti constructor alih-alih [[C0]] ([[A0]]Prototype pollution melalui constructor[[/A0]]).',
    'Node applications can also delete or disable [[C0]] altogether using the command-line flags [[C1]] or [[C2]] respectively. However, this can also be bypassed by using the constructor technique.' => 'Flag Node seperti [[C1]] maupun [[C2]] yang mematikan [[C0]] pun masih dapat dilewati melalui rantai constructor.',
    'Remote code execution via server-side prototype pollution' => 'Eksekusi kode jarak jauh melalui prototype pollution sisi server',
    "While client-side prototype pollution typically exposes the vulnerable website to DOM XSS, server-side prototype pollution can potentially result in remote code execution (RCE). In this section, you'll learn how to identify cases where this may be possible and how to exploit some potential vectors in Node applications." => 'Di lingkungan server Node.js, prototype pollution kerap dapat ditingkatkan menjadi eksekusi kode jarak jauh (RCE).',
    'Identifying a vulnerable request' => 'Mengidentifikasi permintaan yang memicu eksekusi subproses',
    "There are a number of potential command execution sinks in Node, many of which occur in the [[C0]] module. These are often invoked by a request that occurs asynchronously to the request with which you're able to pollute the prototype in the first place. As a result, the best way to identify these requests is by polluting the prototype with a payload that triggers an interaction with Burp Collaborator when called." => 'Sink eksekusi di modul [[C0]] sering berjalan pada endpoint berbeda setelah pencemaran dilakukan, sehingga paling mudah dideteksi memakai pemicu interaksi DNS/HTTP keluar.',
    'The [[C0]] environment variable enables you to define a string of command-line arguments that should be used by default whenever you start a new Node process. As this is also a property on the [[C1]] object, you can potentially control this via prototype pollution if it is undefined.' => 'Variabel lingkungan [[C0]] di objek [[C1]] menentukan argumen baris perintah bawaan setiap kali proses Node baru dijalankan.',
    "Some of Node's functions for creating new child processes accept an optional [[C0]] property, which enables developers to set a specific shell, such as bash, in which to run commands. By combining this with a malicious [[C1]] property, you can pollute the prototype in a way that causes an interaction with Burp Collaborator whenever a new Node process is created:" => 'Dengan menggabungkan properti [[C0]] dan [[C1]], setiap pembuatan subproses akan memanggil domain pemantau eksternal:',
    'This way, you can easily identify when a request creates a new child process with command-line arguments that are controllable via prototype pollution.' => 'Begitu interaksi keluar diterima, Anda tahu permintaan mana yang mengeksekusi child process secara rentan.',
    "The escaped double-quotes in the hostname aren't strictly necessary. However, this can help to reduce false positives by obfuscating the hostname to evade WAFs and other systems that scrape for hostnames." => 'Tanda kutip ter-escape pada nama host membantu menyamarkan domain dari sistem pemindai otomatis.',
    'Remote code execution via child_process.fork()' => 'Eksekusi kode jarak jauh via child_process.fork()',
    "Methods such as [[C0]] and [[C1]] enable developers to create new Node subprocesses. The [[C2]] method accepts an options object in which one of the potential options is the [[C3]] property. This is an array of strings containing command-line arguments that should be used when spawning the child process. If it's left undefined by the developers, this potentially also means it can be controlled via prototype pollution." => 'Fungsi seperti [[C0]] dan [[C1]] menerima properti opsi [[C3]] pada [[C2]] berisi daftar argumen Node untuk subproses baru.',
    "As this gadget lets you directly control the command-line arguments, this gives you access to some attack vectors that wouldn't be possible using [[C0]]. Of particular interest is the [[C1]] argument, which enables you to pass in arbitrary JavaScript that will be executed by the child process. This can be quite powerful, even enabling you to load additional modules into the environment:" => 'Berbeda dari [[C0]], argumen [[C1]] pada array tersebut menjalankan kode JavaScript sembarang termasuk memuat modul sistem di subproses:',
    'In addition to [[C0]], the [[C1]] module contains the [[C2]] method, which executes an arbitrary string as a system command. By chaining these JavaScript and command injection sinks, you can potentially escalate prototype pollution to gain full RCE capability on the server.' => 'Di dalam payload tersebut, pemanggilan metode [[C2]] dari modul [[C1]] di samping [[C0]] langsung mengeksekusi perintah sistem.',
    'Remote code execution via child_process.execSync()' => 'Eksekusi kode jarak jauh via child_process.execSync()',
    'In the previous example, we injected the [[C0]] sink ourselves via the [[C1]] command line argument. In some cases, the application may invoke this method of its own accord in order to execute system commands.' => 'Terkadang aplikasi target sendiri sudah memanggil [[C0]] tanpa perlu suntikan [[C1]].',
    'Just like [[C0]], the [[C1]] method also accepts options object, which may be pollutable via the prototype chain. Although this doesn\'t accept an [[C2]] property, you can still inject system commands into a running child process by simultaneously polluting both the [[C3]] and [[C4]] properties:' => 'Walaupun [[C1]] tidak menerima [[C2]] seperti [[C0]], Anda tetap bisa menyisipkan perintah dengan mencemari [[C3]] dan [[C4]] secara bersamaan:',
    "The [[C0]] option is just a string that is passed to the child process's [[C1]] stream and executed as a system command by [[C2]]. As there are other options for providing the command, such as simply passing it as an argument to the function, the [[C3]] property itself may be left undefined." => 'Opsi [[C0]] mengirim teks langsung ke aliran [[C1]] proses yang dijalankan [[C2]] bila properti [[C3]] tidak diatur.',
    "The [[C0]] option lets developers declare a specific shell in which they want the command to run. By default, [[C1]] uses the system's default shell to run commands, so this may also be left undefined." => 'Opsi [[C0]] menentukan program shell tempat [[C1]] mengeksekusi perintah tersebut.',
    "By polluting both of these properties, you may be able to override the command that the application's developers intended to execute and instead run a malicious command in a shell of your choosing. Note that there are a few caveats to this:" => 'Gabungan kedua properti ini memungkinkan eksekusi perintah pilihan Anda, dengan sejumlah catatan teknis:',
    "The [[C0]] option only accepts the name of the shell's executable and does not allow you to set any additional command-line arguments." => 'Opsi [[C0]] hanya menerima nama berkas eksekusi tanpa argumen tambahan.',
    'The shell is always executed with the [[C0]] argument, which most shells use to let you pass in a command as a string. However, setting the [[C1]] flag in Node instead runs a syntax check on the provided script, which also prevents it from executing. As a result, although there are workarounds for this, it\'s generally tricky to use Node itself as a shell for your attack.' => 'Program shell dipanggil dengan argumen [[C0]]; karena [[C1]] di biner Node hanya memeriksa sintaks, memakai Node langsung kurang efektif.',
    'As the [[C0]] property containing your payload is passed via [[C1]], the shell you choose must accept commands from [[C2]].' => 'Program shell pilihan harus mau membaca perintah dari aliran [[C1]] yang diisi lewat [[C0]] ke [[C2]].',
    "Although they aren't really intended to be shells, the text editors Vim and ex reliably fulfill all of these criteria. If either of these happen to be installed on the server, this creates a potential vector for RCE:" => 'Editor teks Vim maupun ex memenuhi semua syarat tersebut jika terpasang di server:',
    'Vim has an interactive prompt and expects the user to hit [[C0]] to run the provided command. As a result, you need to simulate this by including a newline ([[C1]]) character at the end of your payload, as shown in the example above.' => 'Vim menunggu tombol [[C0]], sehingga sertakan karakter baris baru ([[C1]]) di akhir payload agar perintah langsung dijalankan.',
    'One additional limitation of this technique is that some tools that you might want to use for your exploit also don\'t read data from [[C0]] by default. However, there are a few simple ways around this. In the case of [[C1]], for example, you can read [[C2]] and send the contents as the body of a [[C3]] request using the [[C4]] argument.' => 'Untuk mengekfiltrasi data dengan alat seperti [[C1]] yang tidak membaca [[C0]] atau [[C2]] secara bawaan, kirimkan isi berkas via [[C3]] memakai argumen [[C4]].',
    'In other cases, you can use [[C0]], which converts [[C1]] to a list of arguments that can be passed to a command.' => 'Pada skenario lain, manfaatkan utilitas [[C0]] untuk mengubah aliran [[C1]] menjadi argumen baris perintah.',
    "To help you protect your own websites from the prototype pollution issues we've looked at, we've provided some high-level advice on some of the measures you can take, as well as how to avoid some common pitfalls." => 'Untuk mengamankan aplikasi dari celah prototype pollution, pelajari langkah pencegahannya di halaman berikut:',
    '[[A0]]Preventing prototype pollution vulnerabilities[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Mencegah kerentanan prototype pollution[[/A0]]',

    // Preventing page
    "We recommend patching any prototype pollution vulnerabilities you identify in your websites, regardless of whether these are coupled with exploitable gadgets. Even if you're confident that you haven't missed any, there's no guarantee that future updates to your own code or any libraries you use won't introduce new gadgets, paving the way for viable exploits." => 'Selalu tambal setiap sumber prototype pollution meskipun belum ditemukan gadget aktif, sebab pembaruan kode atau pustaka di masa depan dapat menghadirkan gadget baru.',
    "In this section, we'll provide some high-level advice on some of the measures you can take to protect your own websites from the threats we've covered in our labs. We'll also cover some common pitfalls to avoid." => 'Bagian ini merangkum langkah pertahanan utama beserta kesalahan umum yang perlu dihindari.',
    'Sanitizing property keys' => 'Menyaring kunci properti objek',
    "One of the more obvious ways to prevent prototype pollution vulnerabilities is to sanitize property keys before merging them into existing objects. This way, you can prevent an attacker from injecting keys such as [[C0]], which reference the object's prototype." => 'Menyaring nama kunci masukan mencegah penyuntikan kunci khusus seperti [[C0]] ke operasi penggabungan objek.',
    'Using an allowlist of permitted keys is the most effective way to do this. However, as this is not feasible in many cases, it\'s common to use a blocklist instead, removing any potentially dangerous strings from user input.' => 'Menerapkan daftar putih (allowlist) kunci jauh lebih aman daripada daftar hitam.',
    "Although this is a quick fix to implement, truly robust blocklisting is inherently tricky, as demonstrated by sites that successfully block [[C0]], but fail to account for an attacker [[A0]]polluting an object's prototype via its constructor[[/A0]]. Likewise, weak implementations can also be [[A1]]bypassed using simple obfuscation techniques[[/A1]]. For this reason, we only recommend this as a stopgap rather than a long-term solution." => 'Daftar hitam sulit sempurna karena meski memblokir [[C0]], penyerang tetap bisa [[A0]]mencemari lewat constructor[[/A0]] atau [[A1]]menyamarkan kata kuncinya[[/A1]].',
    'Preventing changes to prototype objects' => 'Mencegah perubahan pada objek prototipe',
    'A more robust approach to preventing prototype pollution vulnerabilities is to prevent prototype objects from being changed at all.' => 'Langkah yang jauh lebih tangguh adalah mengunci objek prototipe agar tidak bisa diubah.',
    'Invoking the [[C0]] method on an object ensures that its properties and their values can no longer be modified, and no new properties can be added. As prototypes are just objects themselves, you can use this method to proactively cut off any potential sources:' => 'Memanggil [[C0]] mencegah modifikasi maupun penambahan properti baru pada prototipe global:',
    'The [[C0]] method is similar, but still allows changes to the values of existing properties. This may be a good compromise if you\'re unable to use [[C1]] for any reason.' => 'Metode [[C0]] menjadi alternatif apabila aplikasi masih perlu mengubah nilai properti yang sudah ada tanpa menambah properti baru seperti pada [[C1]].',
    'Preventing an object from inheriting properties' => 'Mencegah objek mewarisi properti',
    'While you can use [[C0]] to block potential prototype pollution sources, you can also take measures to eliminate gadgets. This way, even if an attacker identifies a prototype pollution vulnerability, it is likely to be unexploitable.' => 'Di samping mengunci sumber lewat [[C0]], Anda juga dapat memutus rantai pewarisan agar gadget tidak berfungsi.',
    "By default, all objects inherit from the global [[C0]] either directly or indirectly via the prototype chain. However, you can also manually set an object's prototype by creating it using the [[C1]] method. Not only does this let you assign any object you like as the new object's prototype, you can also create the object with a [[C2]] prototype, which ensures that it won't inherit any properties at all." => 'Buat objek konfigurasi memakai [[C1]] dengan argumen prototipe [[C2]] agar tidak mewarisi properti dari [[C0]].',
    'Using safer alternatives where possible' => 'Menggunakan struktur data alternatif yang lebih aman',
    'Another robust defense against prototype pollution is to use objects that provide built-in protection. For example, when defining an options object, you could use a [[C0]] instead. Although a map can still inherit malicious properties, they have a built-in [[C1]] method that only returns properties that are defined directly on the map itself:' => 'Struktur [[C0]] menyediakan metode bawaan [[C1]] yang hanya membaca entri miliknya sendiri tanpa terpengaruh rantai prototipe:',
    'A [[C0]] is another alternative if you\'re just storing values rather than [[C1]] pairs. Just like maps, sets provide built-in methods that only return properties that were defined directly on the object itself:' => 'Untuk sekumpulan nilai tanpa pasangan [[C1]], gunakan struktur [[C0]] yang pemeriksaan keanggotaannya juga kebal terhadap pencemaran prototipe:',
];
